[gd_scene format=3]

; The one variable against unit-color-picker-shapes: `color`. Each cell keeps a shape of that
; golden and takes a grey, an HDR colour or a saturated red. A grey has no hue, so the OKHSL hue is
; the float rounding noise of srgb_to_okhsl (thirdparty/misc/ok_color.h), and the OK shapes take
; their stops from it. An HDR colour draws its normalised form (color_picker.cpp:552-565). The
; shapes golden holds one colour, so it shows neither.

